The full merged `hooks` object in `settings.json` becomes:

```json
"hooks": {
  "PreToolUse": [
    {
      "matcher": "Bash",
      "hooks": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "node \"%USERPROFILE%/.claude/scripts/rtk-prerewrite.js\"",
          "async": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "SessionStart": [ ... ],
  "SessionEnd": [ ... ],
  "PostToolUse": [ ... ],
  "UserPromptSubmit": [ ... ],
  "PreCompact": [ ... ],
  "PostCompact": [ ... ],
  "Stop": [ ... ]
}
```

Key design decisions:
- `"async": false` is mandatory. PreToolUse hooks must be synchronous because they must complete before the command executes. An async PreToolUse would race with execution.
- `"matcher": "Bash"` is the correct matcher string for the Bash tool (Claude Code uses the tool name as the matcher literal).
- `%USERPROFILE%` in the command string is resolved by the shell at hook invocation time. On this system that resolves to `C:\Users\nineonelabs003`. Using `%USERPROFILE%` rather than hardcoding makes the hook account-portable.
- Node.js is at `C:\Program Files\nodejs\node` but is in PATH, so `node` resolves without an absolute path.

