## Failure Modes and Fallback Behavior

| Failure mode | Effect | Fallback |
|---|---|---|
| `rtk-prerewrite.js` not found (scripts/ dir missing) | Node exits with error, hook fails | Claude Code's behavior when a PreToolUse hook errors: the tool call proceeds with the **original** unmodified command. RTK discipline rules (AGENTS.md) remain as the backstop. |
| Node.js not in PATH | Same as above | Same fallback. Node is confirmed at `C:\Program Files\nodejs\node` and in PATH (verified: `node --version` = v22.22.1). |
| Malformed JSON from Claude Code | `JSON.parse` throws, caught, `process.exit(0)` | Passthrough — original command runs unchanged. |
| Unexpected `tool_input` shape (no `command` key) | Early exit with `process.exit(0)` | Passthrough. |
| RTK itself not in PATH | Hook rewrites `git status` → `rtk git status`. RTK binary not found → shell error "rtk: command not found" | This is the same failure mode as today if the user manually types `rtk`. Not a regression. RTK is confirmed at v0.36.0. |
| Double-prefix from both hook and manual discipline | `rtk rtk git status` → RTK parses the second `rtk` as a subcommand and fails | Mitigated by the `rest.startsWith('rtk ')` check in `processSegment`. If Claude Code or the user manually types `rtk git status`, the hook detects the prefix and passes through unchanged. |
| `&&` inside quoted string (e.g., commit message) | The quote-aware parser handles double-quoted strings: content inside `"..."` is not split. Single-quoted content is also preserved. | Test: `git commit -m "fix && typo"` → `rtk git commit -m "fix && typo"` (only the outer command gets the prefix; the quoted `&&` is not treated as an operator). |
| `RTK_DISABLED=1 <cmd>` bypass | Hook detects `RTK_DISABLED=1` prefix and returns the segment unchanged. | Escape hatch works as designed. |
| Hook adds latency to every Bash call | Node.js startup (~50-80ms on Windows) × every Bash call = measurable overhead | Acceptable trade-off given RTK's 60-90% token compression. The `async: false` is required for PreToolUse; latency cannot be avoided. For chains of 10+ commands in one Bash call, the overhead is paid once per call, not per segment. |
| `rtk discover` in token-report.ps1 times out | `$ErrorActionPreference = 'SilentlyContinue'` + try/catch means it fails silently | Stop hook still completes; `rtk gain` row still appended. |

